            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "SECTION 5.2. Each employee shall, for the purpose of this Article 5, be regarded as probationary for the first ninety (90) days of employment by the Company, unless mutually agreed by both the Company and the Union to extend the probationary period an additional ninety (90) days, during which period no length of accredited service shall accrue, and Management may terminate employment in its sole discretion. Should the employee continue in the services of the Company after such first ninety (90) days (unless mutually agreed to extend an additional ninety (90) days) and become a regular employee, the length of accredited or continuous service shall then date back to the commencement of such employment.",
            "block_bbox": [
                182,
